          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %em band
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            in which every element is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
          %h2#order_structures_on_bands Order structures on bands
          %p There are two distinct order structures on bands, referred to in the literature by the “natural poset” structure and the “natural preorder” structure.
          %p
            The natural preorder structure is defined by declaring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⪯
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \preceq y
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x y x
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⪯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \preceq
              is reflexive and transitive.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              (This proof appears in a relevant MathStackExchange
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/5074668/43208"} discussion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x x = x x x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              denote an instance of associativity and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              an instance of idempotency. From
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y x = x
              (condition 1) and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y z y = y
              (condition 2), we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi I
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_1 x y x =_2 x y z y x =_I x y(z y x)(z y x) =_A x(y z y)x z y x =_2 x y x z y x =_1 x z y x\qquad(P).
            %p Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi P
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi I
                    %mi x
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi P
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x z x =_P x z(x z y x) =_A (x z)(x z)y x =_I x z y x =_P x
            %p which completes the proof.
          %p
            As is the case with any preorder structure, there is an associated equivalence relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∼
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \sim y
            iff the two conditions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⪯
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \preceq y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⪯
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \preceq x
            hold.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              = succeed "-equivalence" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectangular+band"} rectangular band
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]
              denote the equivalence class of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y, z \in [x]
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y x = x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y z y = y
              (since
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \sim z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              above,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mi y
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x z y x = x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y, z
              are all equivalent, we can equally well say
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mi y
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z y x z = z
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi z
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (z y)x(z y) = z y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z y
              is also in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x]
              is closed under multiplication, and therefore is a band.
            %p
              The rectangularity condition is immediate by definition: for any
              = succeed "-equivalent" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x y x
          %h2#examples_of_bands Examples of bands
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"} semilattice
                (in this article, we mean semilattices without identity) is the same thing as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative"} commutative
                band.
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monoid"} idempotent monoid
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+magma"} unital
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/band"} band
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectangular+band"} rectangular band
                is a band (see there).
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew+lattice"} skew lattice
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L, \wedge, \vee)
                is a band, using either
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∧
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∨
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
                as the semigroup operation.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+ring"} Boolean ring
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                whose multiplication operation is a band.
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicatively+idempotent+semiring"} multiplicatively idempotent semiring
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiring"} semiring
                whose multiplication operation is a band.
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additively+idempotent+semiring"} idempotent semiring
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiring"} semiring
                whose addition operation is a band.
          %p To be added: varieties of bands, and particularly of regular bands.
          %ul
            %li
              A
              %em split band
              is defined in definition 1.1 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#MB78"} McAlister &amp; Blyth 1978
          %h2#relation_to_semilattices Relation to semilattices
          %p
            The category of semilattices is a full subcategory of the category of bands; by general categorical considerations, the full inclusion has a left adjoint, called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflector"} reflector
            from bands to semilattices.
          %p The following result, due to Clifford and Preston, is fundamental.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given a band
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \sim y
              iff
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⪯
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ⪯
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \preceq y) \wedge (y \preceq x)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B/\sim
              is a semilattice, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to B/\sim
              is universal among all maps from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              to semilattices, thus defining the reflector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \mapsto B/\sim
              from bands to semilattices.
          %h2#properties_of_bands Properties of bands
          %p
            By a theorem of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#McLean54"} McLean
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Howie76"} Howie 76, Section IV.4
          %h3#relation_to_rectangular_bands Relation to rectangular bands
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectangular+band"} rectangular band
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/band"} band
                since the defining identity implies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y z = x z
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
                whence by taking
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y=z=x
                one gets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x x = x x
                and from the defining identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x x=x
                hence
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x x = x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y z
                by substituting
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x z x
                for
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi y
                      %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi xy
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi z
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y z = (x z x) y z = x (z (xy) z) = x z \; .
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/band"} band
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                has a decomposition as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{x\in L} R_x
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is a semilattice, each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_x
                is a
                = succeed "-semigroup" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} sub
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi y
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_x R_y \subseteq R_{x y}
                for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of rectangular bands, because we lack connecting morphisms
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_x \to R_y
          %h3#regular_bands Regular bands
          %p
            A band
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            satisfying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphic+category"} graphic identity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y x = x y
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            is said to be
            = succeed "." do
              %em left-regular
            %span.newWikiWord
              random walks
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/random+walk"} ?
            on these hyperplane arrangements by analysing the semigroup algebras of the associated bands: see
            %a{:href => "#Brown00"} Brown 00
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MargolisSaliolaSteinberg15"} Margolis-Saliola-Steinberg 15
            %em graphic monoids
            which are examples of 1-object
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphic+category"} graphic categories
          %h3#skeletons_and_split_bands Skeletons and split bands
          %p
            For the definition of a skeleton of a band, see definition 1.2 of
            %a{:href => "#MB78"} McAlister &amp; Blyth 1978
            for the time being…
          %p
            But according to lemma 1.3 of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MB78"} McAlister &amp; Blyth 1978
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/if+and+only+if"} if and only if
            it has a skeleton.
